WEBVTT

cue0142012
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
The first question of what we studied in the previous weeks, principally.

cue0142013
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.000
In the first dialect, the purpose was to explain the function of tradition.

cue0142014
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
How you cannot have a culture, a nation, a people without a tradition.

cue0142015
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
And therefore, what was the tradition of Israel?

cue0142016
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:37.620
In the second dialogue, he wanted to explain an institution which was maligned principally by Christianity.

cue0142017
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.340
And this is the rabbinical institution.

cue0142018
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:50.620
Until today, there are people who in their mind, they say, well, Judaism is alright, but look at the rabbis.

cue0142019
00:00:50.620 --> 00:01:12.140
And when we examine what the rabbis were, their function, their obligation, what they accomplished, and this is what they did in the second dialogue, we see that no other nation in recorded history was as fortunate as the people of Israel with having the quality of leadership that we had.

cue0142020
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:29.340
And that was the second dialogue. In this dialogue, he wants to analyze not the rabbis as an institution, but the actual accomplishments that they made, what they did, yes?

cue0142021
00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:37.340
And what happened? Different laws, how to explain those laws, not them.

cue0142022
00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:47.340
Alright, we accept them, we understand in general terms, the function, but what is it that they produce?

cue0142023
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:58.340
Now, let me begin myself with a metaphor that I think would illustrate very clearly the rabbinic institutions.

cue0142024
00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:08.440
On the one hand we say what the rabbis do is exactly the way that the Tora prescribed.

cue0142025
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.840
But when historians look into things, there is a difference.

cue0142026
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.460
There are always differences.

cue0142027
00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.240
There are differences.

cue0142028
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.740
So how the rabbis did it?

cue0142029
00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.800
What is it?

cue0142030
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.840
Now I have a beautiful metaphor.

cue0142031
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:39.720
A few, about a hundred and so years ago, there were two brothers, the Wright brothers, who discovered the principle of aerodynamics.

cue0142032
00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:48.540
And they were able to take a monoplane, one single engine plane.

cue0142033
00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:55.440
and I think they were able to fly something like 25 yards and the attitude

cue0142034
00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.540
was something like I don't know 15 or 20 yards right they discovered the

cue0142035
00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:10.660
principle of aerodynamics and they flew for about 25 yards now later on somebody

cue0142036
00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:19.480
says, well that's good. But instead of flying 25 yards, I want to see where I

cue0142037
00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:31.300
could fly a thousand yards. And at an altitude of let's say 100 yards. Now in

cue0142038
00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:39.060
order to produce such a machine, they have to make some changes, all right? Some

cue0142039
00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:46.060
changes in the design of the plane. One minute. Later on somebody says, well, instead of being

cue0142040
00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:53.300
a thousand yards, let's see if we can make it fifty miles. In order to accomplish this,

cue0142041
00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:04.780
you have to redesign the airplane. Eventually somebody says, I want an airplane that I will

cue0142042
00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:15.780
be able to cross the Atlantic. Again, engineering changes and the Atlantic is crossed, etc.,

cue0142043
00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:29.860
etc., etc. A jet plane, 747. Some interplanetary vehicles that we send in orbit around within

cue0142044
00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:37.540
the solar system. Now, there are changes, but the changes do not pertain to the law

cue0142045
00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:43.980
of aerodynamics. It's the same law of aerodynamics. There is no change in the law of aerodynamics.

cue0142046
00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:49.020
But if the same law of aerodynamics tells me that if the vehicle is going to have such

cue0142047
00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:54.020
and such an engine, well, you need such and such a design in order to be able to accomplish

cue0142048
00:04:54.020 --> 00:05:01.260
what you want. The changes are never never to the law itself. The law of aerodynamics,

cue0142049
00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:09.680
nobody could change. This is part of the laws of physics. What we could do is change the

cue0142050
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:16.380
design of our airplanes because what we want today is different than what the Wright brothers

cue0142051
00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:23.640
wanted today. But there is no difference. In a sense, and that's what we're going to

cue0142052
00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:30.280
try to show, and what Rabbi David Nieto tried to show, he didn't use obviously this metaphor,

cue0142053
00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:38.720
this parable, is that the rabbis, the laws of the rabbis, change because the situation

cue0142054
00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.600
of the Jew

cue0142055
00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.540
changed.

cue0142056
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.540
And that situation

cue0142057
00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.440
warranted

cue0142058
00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.300
not a change in the law of the Tora,

cue0142059
00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.460
but a redefining

cue0142060
00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.700
of certain

cue0142061
00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.680
niceties.

cue0142062
00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.640
And let me give you an explanation.

cue0142063
00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.000
There is a controversy

cue0142064
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:01.660
in the Talmud.

cue0142065
00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:03.900
And I brought this example

cue0142066
00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.900
because he discusses it

cue0142067
00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.660
and has been to be in the parasha of this week's parasha.

cue0142068
00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.860
Kitavo. It's something very simple. When Kitavo

cue0142069
00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:17.080
is when you come to the land of Israel and you plant it and so on

cue0142070
00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:21.040
and you have the fruits of your labor

cue0142071
00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.620
so what you should do? You should take Bikurim

cue0142072
00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:28.700
in Spanish Primitias, the first fruits

cue0142073
00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:33.200
of the season, you put it in a basket

cue0142074
00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.000
and you bring it to the temple.

cue0142075
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.760
some miṣva

cue0142076
00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:38.600
some public

cue0142077
00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:42.180
now there is a controversy in the Talmud

cue0142078
00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.560
and the rabbis

cue0142079
00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:45.780
elaborate on this

cue0142080
00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.280
the controversy pertains to the following thing

cue0142081
00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.460
suppose somebody

cue0142082
00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.600
did not sell

cue0142083
00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.020
his land

cue0142084
00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.440
but leased

cue0142085
00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.520
his land to somebody

cue0142086
00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.220
what does it mean that

cue0142087
00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.220
I leased my land

cue0142088
00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.580
the actual real estate belongs to me

cue0142089
00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:12.100
but for X amount of years, you're permitted to work the land,

cue0142090
00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.740
and whatever you harvest belongs to you.

cue0142091
00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:24.760
Still today, the question of leasing property is part of, say, the American legal system.

cue0142092
00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:25.520
We could lease property.

cue0142093
00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.860
The property, when you lease a property for 90 years or 50 years,

cue0142094
00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:31.800
the property does not belong to you.

cue0142095
00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:37.800
But during this 50 years or 90 years, you could erect a building, a factory, whatever it is.

cue0142096
00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:43.800
And there's many business reasons why somebody would prefer to sell, to lease, rather than to sell.

cue0142097
00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:53.800
Now, question. Suppose you lease the land. Now you harvest the fruit.

cue0142098
00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:59.800
And now you come to the primitius, the bikurim, the first fruit.

cue0142099
00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:18.060
Can you take this fruit to the temple? Yes or no? Because when you go to the temple, you have to say thank you to God. And these are the fruits, which you gave to me.

cue0142100
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:35.080
Now, are these my fruits that God gave me? When it says God gave me, meant the fruit only? Or meant the land? Controversy.

cue0142101
00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.960
now what is the nature of this controversy

cue0142102
00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.500
is it that

cue0142103
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.420
something wrong with the Tora

cue0142104
00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.560
whatever the answer is going to be

cue0142105
00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.520
is some invention of the rabbis

cue0142106
00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.620
or is it

cue0142107
00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:52.680
that this kind of buying and selling

cue0142108
00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:57.260
emerged at certain time in history

cue0142109
00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.920
by the end of the second temple

cue0142110
00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.540
and therefore

cue0142111
00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:03.680
the rabbis

cue0142112
00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.660
they have to meet

cue0142113
00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.640
the new situation

cue0142114
00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:08.440
all of a sudden

cue0142115
00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:11.340
we buy and sell differently

cue0142116
00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.540
and because we buy and sell differently

cue0142117
00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.060
we change

cue0142118
00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:18.600
we have to know

cue0142119
00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.180
how to apply the law of the Tora

cue0142120
00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.200
it's just like I say

cue0142121
00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.620
well I want an airplane

cue0142122
00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:27.760
that will be able to carry

cue0142123
00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:28.860
such and such a load

cue0142124
00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:31.680
and therefore I have to figure out

cue0142125
00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.400
for such and such a load

cue0142126
00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:37.560
what kind of engine I need to design, etc., etc.

cue0142127
00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:45.020
So the principal point of the controversy

cue0142128
00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.340
or the innovations of the rabbis,

cue0142129
00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.280
so somebody says,

cue0142130
00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:52.480
this is a ridiculous controversy, who cares?

cue0142131
00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:53.580
No, no.

cue0142132
00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:54.920
The sense is,

cue0142133
00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.780
you gave me, you have to say you gave me.

cue0142134
00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.040
You gave it to, is it his or not?

cue0142135
00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:02.660
Do you understand the problem?

cue0142136
00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:07.440
Let me give you another problem.

cue0142137
00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:12.400
Also at the end of the second temple.

cue0142138
00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:17.040
And I want you to see the problems discussed by the rabbis.

cue0142139
00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:19.820
And the nature of these problems.

cue0142140
00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.220
If a person made a vow.

cue0142141
00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:26.880
To bring a Qorban.

cue0142142
00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.440
A sacrifice.

cue0142143
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:30.940
To the temple.

cue0142144
00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:45.600
the first holiday, the first of the three holidays, which are Pesaḥ, Shaḇuʿot, and Sukkot, he should bring them.

cue0142145
00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:53.660
If three holidays pass, and he didn't bring them, he made a sin.

cue0142146
00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:54.740
Balteacher.

cue0142147
00:10:54.740 --> 00:11:24.720
hair. Now, problem in the Talmud. What happens if a person dies? He may, such as this sheep, goat, whatever it is, it's going to be a Qorban for the temple. The person dies. His children inherit his property.

cue0142148
00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:29.260
do the children have the obligation

cue0142149
00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:32.140
to bring this animal to the temple

cue0142150
00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:35.320
and suppose

cue0142151
00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:38.300
they did not bring the animal to her temple

cue0142152
00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:42.520
and three holidays elapsed

cue0142153
00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.100
are they committing a sin?

cue0142154
00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:48.120
discussion with the rabbis

cue0142155
00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.720
rabbinical institutions

cue0142156
00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:51.960
what happened?

cue0142157
00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:54.640
what happened is

cue0142158
00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.380
something that didn't happen before to us

cue0142159
00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.140
at the end of the second temple

cue0142160
00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:02.900
hundreds of thousands of Jews were killed

cue0142161
00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:03.580
were massacred

cue0142162
00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:07.220
and therefore this problem

cue0142163
00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:11.820
became a burning problem

cue0142164
00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.040
what to do?

cue0142165
00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:16.760
so as

cue0142166
00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:19.760
new situations

cue0142167
00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.400
as our socio-political

cue0142168
00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.000
economic situation

cue0142169
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:25.820
changed

cue0142170
00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.920
abruptly.

cue0142171
00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:31.240
New problems

cue0142172
00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.180
came about.

cue0142173
00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.120
And when those

cue0142174
00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.220
problems came about,

cue0142175
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:38.760
the rabbis

cue0142176
00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.140
had to give

cue0142177
00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:41.640
solutions.

cue0142178
00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:44.220
Now, a principle

cue0142179
00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:47.520
which is fundamental

cue0142180
00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:52.240
there are controversies among the rabbis

cue0142181
00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.320
and we want to see what brought about

cue0142182
00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:55.200
these controversies

cue0142183
00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:59.940
but following and citing my manners

cue0142184
00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.320
Rabbi David Nieto says

cue0142185
00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.560
every controversy that we had

cue0142186
00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.340
in the Talmud

cue0142187
00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:09.860
pertain not to the substance

cue0142188
00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:11.160
to the akkar

cue0142189
00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.400
to the principle of the law

cue0142190
00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:16.880
but only to details

cue0142191
00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:18.900
details

cue0142192
00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.480
details that arouse

cue0142193
00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.840
because new circumstances

cue0142194
00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.400
arouse

cue0142195
00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.880
example

cue0142196
00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:29.160
now we lease land

cue0142197
00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.240
it's a new situation

cue0142198
00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.020
new situation

cue0142199
00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:35.540
we know the law

cue0142200
00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.340
what the law says

cue0142201
00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.660
the law says only the proprietor

cue0142202
00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:41.360
may come and bring

cue0142203
00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:43.400
but we do not know

cue0142204
00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.480
whether the proprietor means the proprietor of the fruits

cue0142205
00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:47.780
or the proprietor of the real estate.

cue0142206
00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:52.300
We know that the Baʿal,

cue0142207
00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.520
the owner, the proprietor of the Qorban,

cue0142208
00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:56.640
has to bring it to the temple.

cue0142209
00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:58.960
We know that the proprietor,

cue0142210
00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:01.100
if he doesn't bring it, makes a sin.

cue0142211
00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.560
But now the children are the proprietor.

cue0142212
00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.320
Do they make a sin or not?

cue0142213
00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.980
The controversies of the rabbis

cue0142214
00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:14.760
pertain only to the details.

cue0142215
00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:23.960
let me give you another example we all say Shemaʿ Israel of my heart now in this

cue0142216
00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:29.580
I can't explain how do we say this Shemaʿ

cue0142217
00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:37.380
the Chama and I don't know about a bit of on says it's written the shock

cue0142218
00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:39.420
V'shokvecha uv kumecha.

cue0142219
00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.420
V'shokvecha means

cue0142220
00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.800
when you are about to sleep

cue0142221
00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.160
and when you get up.

cue0142222
00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:49.580
And they say, you know what it means?

cue0142223
00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:51.640
That at night,

cue0142224
00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:53.860
you have to sit down when you say God'shema.

cue0142225
00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:57.740
And in the morning,

cue0142226
00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:00.620
uv kumecha,

cue0142227
00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.100
you say the God'shema standing up.

cue0142228
00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.240
V'shokvecha uv kumecha.

cue0142229
00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.100
comes Bet Hillel,

cue0142230
00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:11.220
say no, no, no, no.

cue0142231
00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:13.860
Besokbecha means

cue0142232
00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:17.100
at the time that you're going to go to sleep.

cue0142233
00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.100
Ufkumecha means

cue0142234
00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.880
at the time

cue0142235
00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:25.540
that you get up in the morning.

cue0142236
00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:27.600
Now pay attention.

cue0142237
00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.780
The controversy

cue0142238
00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.220
does not pertain

cue0142239
00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.920
to the substance of the law.

cue0142240
00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:35.380
Namely,

cue0142241
00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:38.620
every male Jew

cue0142242
00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.560
must recite Kiryat Shemaʿ

cue0142243
00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.900
once in the morning and once at night.

cue0142244
00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:44.360
There are no controversies

cue0142245
00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.400
pertaining to the substance of the law.

cue0142246
00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:49.880
The controversies that you find in the Talmud

cue0142247
00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:54.740
apply to details.

cue0142248
00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.380
What he calls Se'ifim,

cue0142249
00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.000
secondary circumstances of the law.

cue0142250
00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:10.060
Now, why there were controversies?

cue0142251
00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:12.540
What happened?

cue0142252
00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:16.320
Very important thing.

cue0142253
00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:20.980
We Jews, much before the Romans,

cue0142254
00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.940
certainly much before the United States of America,

cue0142255
00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.020
we had a judicial system.

cue0142256
00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:33.680
And people forget that we had also a system

cue0142257
00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:39.000
whereby you could appeal a law.

cue0142258
00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:46.200
Namely, we had, principally we had three kinds of courts.

cue0142259
00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.320
I want you to remember this.

cue0142260
00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:54.300
You had a court of three judges,

cue0142261
00:16:55.020 --> 00:17:02.080
and this court cannot deal with criminal law,

cue0142262
00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:08.020
only with business law,

cue0142263
00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.880
with monetary law,

cue0142264
00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:13.000
but not with criminal law.

cue0142265
00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:14.680
If I hit somebody,

cue0142266
00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.340
which is a crime in Jewish law,

cue0142267
00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.580
if I kill somebody,

cue0142268
00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.080
anything which involves a crime,

cue0142269
00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:25.620
this court of three cannot deal with it.

cue0142270
00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:28.580
So you had one court of three.

cue0142271
00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:31.880
Then you had courts,

cue0142272
00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:47.040
of 23 members. And this court could deal with criminal matters, and if needed be, they could even apply capital punishment.

cue0142273
00:17:47.040 --> 00:18:10.560
And then, there was the Bet Din, the Sanhedrin, which were seated at the Bet HaMikdash, had 71 members, and it deal not only with criminal law, but political law.

cue0142274
00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.280
they could even summon the king

cue0142275
00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.300
and trial the king

cue0142276
00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:20.200
in their Jewish system

cue0142277
00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.400
the king

cue0142278
00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:23.260
is subject to the law

cue0142279
00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:25.380
the supreme court

cue0142280
00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.740
can summon a king

cue0142281
00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.040
alright

cue0142282
00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:29.760
now

cue0142283
00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:34.520
up to the destruction of the temple

cue0142284
00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:38.560
there were no controversies among the Jewish people

cue0142285
00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:40.260
why?

cue0142286
00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:52.520
Whenever there was a controversy among the different courts throughout Israel, throughout the Jewish diaspora, the matter would be appealed.

cue0142287
00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:55.160
And it would go to the court of 23.

cue0142288
00:18:56.540 --> 00:19:07.320
If there was a dispute among the courts of 23, you further appeal this matter and you bring it to the Supreme Court.

cue0142289
00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:09.480
and the Supreme Court

cue0142290
00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:12.520
will give a final decision.

cue0142291
00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.420
And that would be the law.

cue0142292
00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.760
With the destruction of the temple,

cue0142293
00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.360
we no longer have a Supreme Court.

cue0142294
00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:28.140
Now, suppose there is a bad deed in Tiberia.

cue0142295
00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:31.860
It says,

cue0142296
00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:33.340
this is permitted.

cue0142297
00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:44.560
When you have a Bet Din in Caesarea or in Baḇel, that says something different.

cue0142298
00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:59.380
You have no legal means to summon the parties and to force them to come to an agreement.

cue0142299
00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:06.380
So one says, mutar, permissible.

cue0142300
00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:10.900
The other says what? It's forbidden.

cue0142301
00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:20.880
And because we did not have a central authority, a central judicial authority,

cue0142302
00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:25.300
there was no means

cue0142303
00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:29.260
by which to determine

cue0142304
00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:33.040
what the law is.

cue0142305
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:35.660
And because

cue0142306
00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:44.660
There were students

cue0142307
00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:47.620
who misunderstood the teachers.

cue0142308
00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:49.860
Because the teachers used different words.

cue0142309
00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:54.360
And they thought that their respective teachers were in disagreement with each other.

cue0142310
00:20:56.600 --> 00:21:02.520
And because of this, there was a lot of controversy among the Jewish people.

cue0142311
00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:10.440
Imagine America, United States of America, without a Supreme Court.

cue0142312
00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:19.620
how many minutes, hours, days, maybe weeks

cue0142313
00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:23.760
will pass before there will break civil war between the states.

cue0142314
00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:28.280
The miracle that happened

cue0142315
00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:32.300
is that in spite of the controversy,

cue0142316
00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:36.360
without a central force,

cue0142317
00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:40.000
with authority

cue0142318
00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.680
to say to the courts

cue0142319
00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:43.560
come before us

cue0142320
00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.900
present your case

cue0142321
00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.520
and we'll decide

cue0142322
00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:51.800
still

cue0142323
00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.520
the Jewish people

cue0142324
00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:56.360
were able to

cue0142325
00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:59.720
solve the situations

cue0142326
00:21:59.720 --> 00:22:01.840
and to minimize

cue0142327
00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:05.640
the controversies

cue0142328
00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:14.240
Now, I will explain more, but before, let me tell you something that he asked.

cue0142329
00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:19.360
He said, well, something is strange among the Jewish people.

cue0142330
00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:25.840
We always say that those rabbis that were for us, they have more authority than we do.

cue0142331
00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:30.100
Well, why?

cue0142332
00:22:30.100 --> 00:22:43.280
we see that throughout our history, throughout history, the later authorities know more than the preceding authorities.

cue0142333
00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:56.080
And he brings as an example the great, great progress made in science in the 17th century,

cue0142334
00:22:56.080 --> 00:23:00.000
where I was living, in the field of astronomy, in the field of medicine.

cue0142335
00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:08.220
So he says, how could you say that the preceding rabbis knew more than us today?

cue0142336
00:23:10.340 --> 00:23:15.940
When we see that the whole world is always the newer generation,

cue0142337
00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:20.080
knows more than the preceding generation.

cue0142338
00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:21.300
You understand the question you're asking?

cue0142339
00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:25.980
He says, we should be able to solve the problems that the Ḥakhamim in the Talmud says.

cue0142340
00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:28.260
Because we are more intelligent.

cue0142341
00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:29.220
We know more.

cue0142342
00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.740
There is a progress in the development of the human brain.

cue0142343
00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:35.340
So you're going to tell me that,

cue0142344
00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:37.800
Rishonim kamal achim, Rishonim al-gai angels,

cue0142345
00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:39.620
and we are just like human beings.

cue0142346
00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:41.520
Because we see that this is not a fact.

cue0142347
00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:44.720
How to answer this question?

cue0142348
00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:47.140
Now he gives an answer.

cue0142349
00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:50.160
And I'll be frank with you.

cue0142350
00:23:51.680 --> 00:23:54.860
I would not have been able to understand that answer

cue0142351
00:23:54.860 --> 00:23:58.940
will not be because of the fact that I read another book.

cue0142352
00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:02.740
And through the other book, which I'll tell you in a minute about it,

cue0142353
00:24:03.280 --> 00:24:08.000
I was able to understand what Rabbi David Nieto was talking all about.

cue0142354
00:24:10.180 --> 00:24:12.380
He says, Rabbi David Nieto is...

cue0142355
00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:14.700
No, we are more intelligent than the preceding one.

cue0142356
00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:21.000
Modern man sees, understands things that the ancients weren't capable of.

cue0142357
00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:28.400
Imagine I would tell to somebody 80 years ago about that space and time are relative.

cue0142358
00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:35.720
The person will not be able to understand the simple notion of what a college boy knows today through Einstein,

cue0142359
00:24:35.880 --> 00:24:37.540
that relativity of time and space.

cue0142360
00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:42.620
They want to be able just to understand the concept, let alone the mathematics.

cue0142361
00:24:42.740 --> 00:24:43.760
They want to be able to understand it.

cue0142362
00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:48.480
Or a person in the 16th century could not understand calculus, would not be possible.

cue0142363
00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:51.800
The brain could not grasp calculus.

cue0142364
00:24:52.140 --> 00:24:52.940
It would be impossible.

cue0142365
00:24:53.860 --> 00:24:55.560
And today, as we progress,

cue0142366
00:24:56.880 --> 00:24:58.580
we see that the human brain

cue0142367
00:24:58.580 --> 00:25:01.680
is developing at a fantastic pace.

cue0142368
00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:06.420
Now he says, give this following answer.

cue0142369
00:25:07.180 --> 00:25:08.380
And I will try to explain it to you.

cue0142370
00:25:09.340 --> 00:25:12.120
He says, the reason that we don't know Tora

cue0142371
00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:16.180
as much as the Pacific ones

cue0142372
00:25:16.180 --> 00:25:17.780
is not because we are less intelligent.

cue0142373
00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:21.140
but because we are in Galut

cue0142374
00:25:21.140 --> 00:25:25.380
because we are in Galut

cue0142375
00:25:25.380 --> 00:25:27.160
we know

cue0142376
00:25:27.160 --> 00:25:28.860
we can know mathematics more than them

cue0142377
00:25:28.860 --> 00:25:31.000
biology, I don't know

cue0142378
00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:32.640
microphysics

cue0142379
00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:34.800
everything is, yeah, but Torano

cue0142380
00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:36.060
we cannot know because we are in Galut

cue0142381
00:25:36.060 --> 00:25:38.560
what does it mean?

cue0142382
00:25:40.660 --> 00:25:41.060
again

cue0142383
00:25:41.060 --> 00:25:45.300
Rabbi Davin Neto is very dear to me

cue0142384
00:25:45.300 --> 00:25:46.240
I've been very confident

cue0142385
00:25:46.240 --> 00:25:47.880
for many years

cue0142386
00:25:47.880 --> 00:25:51.000
There is another Rabbi that I...

cue0142387
00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:57.860
I'm sure that you have your favorite, I don't know, musicians or philosophers or playwrights or so on.

cue0142388
00:25:57.980 --> 00:25:59.380
So I have my favorite Ḥakhamim.

cue0142389
00:26:00.500 --> 00:26:02.560
I have a special list.

cue0142390
00:26:02.560 --> 00:26:08.260
And one of them is called Rabbi Yoseph Yavis Hehasid.

cue0142391
00:26:09.500 --> 00:26:15.280
He was one of the Jews who left not Spain, but Portugal.

cue0142392
00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:17.380
He was from Galut, Portugal.

cue0142393
00:26:17.880 --> 00:26:25.880
And he left Portugal about 1507, around that time, right at the beginning of the 1500s.

cue0142394
00:26:25.880 --> 00:26:31.880
Now, he was an extraordinary man. He's called a Ḥasid because he was just a devout and pious man.

cue0142395
00:26:31.880 --> 00:26:39.880
And he wrote innumerable kinds of books. And above all, when he reached Saloniki, he established a printing press.

cue0142396
00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:43.100
I think he belonged to a wealthy family.

cue0142397
00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:51.000
And many, many books printed in Saloniki came out from the house of Rabbi Yoseph Yaris.

cue0142398
00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:54.940
Eventually, the family moved to Egypt.

cue0142399
00:26:56.400 --> 00:27:03.300
And I knew one of the descendants, who was one of the great poets of our time,

cue0142400
00:27:03.380 --> 00:27:06.120
he just died a few years ago, Edmond Javis.

cue0142401
00:27:06.120 --> 00:27:07.560
One of the great poets.

cue0142402
00:27:07.560 --> 00:27:11.040
somebody wrote in France that there is no modern poet

cue0142403
00:27:11.040 --> 00:27:13.100
in France who was not directly influenced

cue0142404
00:27:13.100 --> 00:27:14.480
by the poetry of Edmond Chavez

cue0142405
00:27:14.480 --> 00:27:17.140
a very good Jew and he passed away

cue0142406
00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:18.380
so his

cue0142407
00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:20.520
ancestor, the Biossef

cue0142408
00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:21.320
he says like this

cue0142409
00:27:21.320 --> 00:27:24.120
once he was summoned

cue0142410
00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:25.980
by the king of Portugal

cue0142411
00:27:25.980 --> 00:27:28.900
and he says

cue0142412
00:27:28.900 --> 00:27:29.880
the king in Portugal

cue0142413
00:27:29.880 --> 00:27:32.940
I want to ask you a question

cue0142414
00:27:32.940 --> 00:27:35.780
how do you say

cue0142415
00:27:35.780 --> 00:27:38.720
that when the Mashiaḥ will come,

cue0142416
00:27:39.680 --> 00:27:42.120
you will be able

cue0142417
00:27:42.120 --> 00:27:46.840
to be the most powerful kingdom on earth.

cue0142418
00:27:46.920 --> 00:27:47.600
When I see you,

cue0142419
00:27:47.820 --> 00:27:49.960
you are the drag of everybody.

cue0142420
00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:51.960
You are the lowest of the lowest.

cue0142421
00:27:52.500 --> 00:27:53.500
How can you do that?

cue0142422
00:27:53.720 --> 00:27:54.480
How could you say that?

cue0142423
00:27:56.520 --> 00:27:57.540
Rabbi Yoseph Yavis writes

cue0142424
00:27:57.540 --> 00:27:58.660
that at the time he didn't know the answer.

cue0142425
00:27:58.740 --> 00:27:59.560
He didn't have the final answer.

cue0142426
00:27:59.680 --> 00:28:00.360
He didn't know what to answer.

cue0142427
00:28:01.620 --> 00:28:04.140
And as they were asking him the question,

cue0142428
00:28:04.140 --> 00:28:09.060
the slaves, the servants of the king, they come

cue0142429
00:28:09.060 --> 00:28:11.620
and they announce to him

cue0142430
00:28:11.620 --> 00:28:16.260
that once they had captured

cue0142431
00:28:16.260 --> 00:28:18.400
two cubs, two lion cubs,

cue0142432
00:28:18.620 --> 00:28:20.580
wild lions, you know, they're not real lions,

cue0142433
00:28:20.680 --> 00:28:22.920
I mean, something like the jaguars,

cue0142434
00:28:23.160 --> 00:28:26.360
those wild cats in Europe.

cue0142435
00:28:27.100 --> 00:28:30.120
And they had captured

cue0142436
00:28:30.120 --> 00:28:33.180
two wild baby cubs

cue0142437
00:28:33.180 --> 00:28:36.480
they put the collar to each of them

cue0142438
00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:38.940
and they raised them for about

cue0142439
00:28:38.940 --> 00:28:40.260
I don't know, a year or so on

cue0142440
00:28:40.260 --> 00:28:42.340
and then one of them

cue0142441
00:28:42.340 --> 00:28:45.040
managed to escape

cue0142442
00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:47.140
and at the moment

cue0142443
00:28:47.140 --> 00:28:49.200
that the king was asking the question

cue0142444
00:28:49.200 --> 00:28:50.820
to Rabbi Yoseph Yavis

cue0142445
00:28:50.820 --> 00:28:53.880
his slaves told him

cue0142446
00:28:53.880 --> 00:28:56.520
that they recaptured after X amount of years

cue0142447
00:28:56.520 --> 00:28:58.380
the brother

cue0142448
00:28:58.380 --> 00:29:01.500
when they captured

cue0142449
00:29:01.500 --> 00:29:04.880
the king and everybody else saw

cue0142450
00:29:04.880 --> 00:29:06.400
that this brother

cue0142451
00:29:06.400 --> 00:29:09.420
was much larger

cue0142452
00:29:09.420 --> 00:29:13.120
had more

cue0142453
00:29:13.120 --> 00:29:14.940
more courage

cue0142454
00:29:14.940 --> 00:29:17.340
stronger

cue0142455
00:29:17.340 --> 00:29:19.120
wilder

cue0142456
00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:21.560
than his brother

cue0142457
00:29:21.560 --> 00:29:25.200
and the Biosphere

cue0142458
00:29:25.200 --> 00:29:27.640
caught the thing on the spot

cue0142459
00:29:27.640 --> 00:29:29.100
and he says

cue0142460
00:29:29.100 --> 00:29:29.820
my lord

cue0142461
00:29:29.820 --> 00:29:31.780
how could you explain

cue0142462
00:29:31.780 --> 00:29:34.120
two twin brothers

cue0142463
00:29:34.120 --> 00:29:36.680
one seems so shy

cue0142464
00:29:36.680 --> 00:29:38.380
and so weak and so

cue0142465
00:29:38.380 --> 00:29:39.120
passive

cue0142466
00:29:39.120 --> 00:29:41.600
and the other

cue0142467
00:29:41.600 --> 00:29:44.540
so strong

cue0142468
00:29:44.540 --> 00:29:45.980
so virile

cue0142469
00:29:45.980 --> 00:29:47.480
what's the meaning?

cue0142470
00:29:49.900 --> 00:29:50.400
and the king says

cue0142471
00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:51.060
no problem

cue0142472
00:29:51.060 --> 00:29:53.660
because this second one

cue0142473
00:29:53.660 --> 00:29:55.880
he lived in the wilderness

cue0142474
00:29:55.880 --> 00:29:59.820
natural habitat

cue0142475
00:29:59.820 --> 00:30:02.880
and therefore was able to develop

cue0142476
00:30:02.880 --> 00:30:05.580
whereas this is a prisoner

cue0142477
00:30:05.580 --> 00:30:07.580
says king

cue0142478
00:30:07.580 --> 00:30:09.980
this is our answer

cue0142479
00:30:09.980 --> 00:30:13.120
you see us now

cue0142480
00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:15.180
at the bottom of society

cue0142481
00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:19.140
because we are in prison

cue0142482
00:30:19.140 --> 00:30:25.000
but when we are going to break out of prison

cue0142483
00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:27.620
and to roam

cue0142484
00:30:27.620 --> 00:30:30.980
through our natural habitat.

cue0142485
00:30:32.980 --> 00:30:35.620
We are not going to be like we are now.

cue0142486
00:30:36.860 --> 00:30:39.020
We're going to fully develop

cue0142487
00:30:39.020 --> 00:30:43.080
and then, yes,

cue0142488
00:30:44.020 --> 00:30:48.140
we will be the most powerful nation on earth.

cue0142489
00:30:49.420 --> 00:30:50.920
Because of this story,

cue0142490
00:30:51.460 --> 00:30:52.520
I understood, Rabbi,

cue0142491
00:30:52.520 --> 00:30:55.940
David Nieto.

cue0142492
00:30:57.220 --> 00:30:59.280
We could be intelligent in every single

cue0142493
00:30:59.280 --> 00:31:00.280
facet in the world.

cue0142494
00:31:01.680 --> 00:31:03.380
But as long as we

cue0142495
00:31:03.380 --> 00:31:05.460
are not growing in a natural

cue0142496
00:31:05.460 --> 00:31:07.120
Jewish habitat,

cue0142497
00:31:07.980 --> 00:31:11.380
